From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 02:50:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] Verify the signed-in path and WIC against the real
 account
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The owner scanned the login QR. What the self-test recorded, verbatim:

  === signed in: mid 364662067, room 1738567607 ===
  [signed-in FetchRoom]             ok roomId=1738567607 areaId=1062 title=干活，写文
  [signed-in LoadShieldKeywords]    ok, 0 keywords
  [signed-in IsIdentifiedByFaceAuth] ok, identified=true
  [signed-in LoadEmoticons]         ok, {"packs":[{"key":"upower_[doge_金箍]",...}]}

So 扫码登录 and 拉到房间信息 are both live-verified now, not request-verified:
the session went through the page's own QR code into `ready`, and FetchRoom
walked the room_id_by_uid leg that needs an account. The run happened twice and
the second one read liveStatus=1 where the first read 0.

WIC is verified too, and cleanly: after the login the emote picker pulled the
room's emotes and the cache holds 225 files, of which **225 carry the PNG magic
and 0 do not**, with **0 of them over 160 px** in their IHDR. That is exactly
what Emoticons.swift:203-214 asks for — the encoder ran on every picture, the
scaler bounded every one, and not a single container fell back to the raw
bytes. The remaining gap I recorded last commit is closed.

The self-test's room picker now takes the busiest entry rather than the first,
and prefers room 5050 when get_info says it is streaming. `online` is a heat
value: the hottest room in the recommend list was sending four danmaku a minute,
which proves the socket and exercises nothing downstream of it.

Nothing was written to the account: LIVEHIME_SELFTEST_WRITE stayed unset, so
UpdateTitle, SendDanmaku, StartLive and StopLive have still not run against it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 plugins/livehime/core/win/livehime-core.cpp | 45 ++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plugins/livehime/core/win/livehime-core.cpp b/plugins/livehime/core/win/livehime-core.cpp
index a5ac6de..bb26381 100644
--- a/plugins/livehime/core/win/livehime-core.cpp
+++ b/plugins/livehime/core/win/livehime-core.cpp
@@ -176,21 +176,54 @@ void SelfTest()
 		nlohmann::json parsed = nlohmann::json::parse(response.body, nullptr, false);
 		line("[liveList] status=" + std::to_string(response.status) + " code=" +
 		     std::to_string(parsed.is_discarded() ? -999 : parsed.value("code", -999)));
+		/* The busiest entry, not the first one. `online` is a heat value, not a
+		 * viewer count, and the first entry of this list turned out to be a
+		 * room that answers with one or two danmaku a minute — enough to prove
+		 * the socket works and not enough to exercise the parts that only run
+		 * when someone actually chats. */
+		long long best_online = 0;
 		if (!parsed.is_discarded() && parsed.contains("data") && parsed["data"].is_array()) {
 			for (const auto &entry : parsed["data"]) {
 				const long long id = entry.value("roomid", 0LL);
 				const long long online = entry.value("online", 0LL);
-				if (id > 0 && online > 0) {
+				if (id > 0 && online > best_online) {
+					best_online = online;
 					live_room = id;
-					line("[liveList] using room " + std::to_string(id) + " online=" +
-					     std::to_string(online) + " title=" +
-					     entry.value("title", std::string()).substr(0, 40));
-					break;
 				}
 			}
 		}
-		if (live_room == 1)
+		if (live_room != 1)
+			line("[liveList] busiest is room " + std::to_string(live_room) + " online=" +
+			     std::to_string(best_online));
+		else
 			line("[liveList] no live room found; falling back to room 1");
+
+		/* `online` is a heat value and the hottest room in this list turned out
+		 * to send four danmaku a minute, which proves the socket and exercises
+		 * nothing downstream of it. Room 5050 is a known-loud room: take it
+		 * when get_info says it is actually streaming (live_status 1), and say
+		 * which one was chosen either way so a quiet run is never mistaken for
+		 * a broken one. */
+		{
+			livehime::net::Request probe;
+			probe.url = livehime::net::AppendQuery(
+				"https://api.live.bilibili.com/room/v1/Room/get_info", "room_id=5050");
+			probe.headers["User-Agent"] =
+				"Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 14_0) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like "
+				"Gecko) Version/17.0 Safari/605.1.15";
+			probe.headers["Referer"] = "https://live.bilibili.com/";
+			nlohmann::json p2 =
+				nlohmann::json::parse(livehime::net::SendSync(probe).body, nullptr, false);
+			const int status = p2.is_discarded()
+						   ? -1
+						   : p2.value("data", nlohmann::json::object())
+							     .value("live_status", -1);
+			line("[liveList] room 5050 live_status=" + std::to_string(status));
+			if (status == 1) {
+				live_room = 5050;
+				line("[liveList] using the known-loud room 5050 instead");
+			}
+		}
 	}
 
